meta {
  name: Import Steam Wishlist (Stream)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{backendUrl}}/api/user/steam/wishlist/import/stream
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  [
    {
      "appid": 620
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  SSE variant of a wishlist import - same event shape and caveat as
  "Import Steam Library (Stream)": a plain HTTP request just returns
  the raw event-stream body once the connection closes, not live
  progress. Sends the wishlist items (appid only is required;
  priority/date_added are ignored) as the JSON body, so the import
  always matches what "Preview Steam Wishlist" showed. Each created
  entry gets status "Not Owned" and owned=false.

  Run auth/Login and user/Set Steam ID first. A missing Steam ID
  surfaces as an `error` event inside an HTTP 200 stream, not as a
  400. An appid below 1 or a list over 10000 items is a plain 400
  before the stream opens.
}